  "live_records": {
    "q-224463": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224463",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.26.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6} \\\\  & ≈0.1642.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1})(0.26)^{1}(1-0.26)^{6-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6}+6\\cdot (0.26)^{1}\\cdot (0.74)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.5104.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
