    "q-224505": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224505",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.65).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $0.0018$ | $0.0223$ | $0.1174$ | $0.3529$ | $0.6809$ | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.65.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =0.6809+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.65)^{5}(1-0.65)^{6-5} \\\\  & =0.6809+6\\cdot (0.65)^{5}\\cdot (0.35)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9246.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
