    "q-224517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224517",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.85)$ given below, compute $P(X<5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0000\\,$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0012\\,$ | $\\,0.0121\\,$ | $\\,0.0738\\,$ | $\\,0.2834\\,$ | $\\,0.6794\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4) \\\\  & =0.0738.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
