    "q-225125": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225125",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.8)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0016\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0989\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.7379\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(0) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.0001 \\\\  & =0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
