    "q-225190": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225190",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.79)$ given below, compute $P(X>3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0004\\,$ | $\\,0.0081\\,$ | $\\,0.0659\\,$ | $\\,0.2833\\,$ | $\\,0.6923\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.2833 \\\\  & =0.7167.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
